+# Quartet decay: personal N1–N8 scope review
+
+No broad obstruction or axiom update is established. A supplied continuum
+phase has calculable leading-order decay channels when its cones differ.
+
+## N1 — Routes actually tested
+
+| Family | Work performed | Disposition |
+|---|---|---|
+| Convex dispersion geometry | Compare energy differences and the exact two-body minimum | Exact strict group-velocity and phase-velocity thresholds |
+| Fermion angular cap | Integrate the energy delta before the angular variables | General positive-coframe rate integral |
+| Isotropic phase space | Integrate a scalar polynomial with and without photon-energy weight | Distinct number rate and emitted power |
+| Anisotropic photon tensor | Rescale momenta and integrate actual Pauli projectors | Closed positive polarization matrix; Weyl multiplicity retained |
+| Generic angular asymptotics | Rescale the narrow emission cap with a fixed angular margin | Leading quartet contrast rates |
+| Angular-boundary escape | Derive the shear cap disk and integrate its rational kernel | Nonzero second-order emission where the linear contrast vanishes |
+| Literature comparison | Match the massless small-deformation coefficients in the primary source | Established mechanism credited, no fitted bound imported |
+
+These are derivations and challenges within one specified action, not seven
+independent proofs that the microscopic interacting phase exists.
+
+## N2 — Dependence
+
+All rates rely on the same supplied massless cone and Maxwell action. The
+quartet application also relies on Blocks11–13. Hall cancellation, metric
+attraction and a small decay rate cannot be counted as independent evidence
+for a selected physical phase or an isolated charged pole.
+
+## N3 — Premises and thresholds
+
+Zero density, a filled negative band, canonically normalized transverse
+photons, separated untilted Weyl cones and leading coupling order are explicit.
+The strict photon and fermion thresholds use different velocities. Equality
+surfaces and limits without the angular margin are not covered by the generic
+linear asymptotic. The exact shear boundary example is a supplied coframe;
+the actual quartet needs its second-order photon metric and polarization there.
+
+## N4 — Source match
+
+The current native coframe and Hall-free quartet sources supply the action,
+node count and real beta-function comparators. Their continuum matching does
+not supply an interacting ground state. The primary Lorentz-violating QED
+paper uses different finite-deformation conventions; only the matched leading
+massless coefficients are compared. No empirical number is used.
+
+## N5 — Resolution and failures
+
+Exact symbolic scalar integrals, actual Pauli matrix traces, a separate full
+photon phase-space integration, cap refinement and an analytic boundary
+integral challenge sensitive signs and factors. The first momentum-triangle
+cancellation and insufficient angular quadrature are frozen with diagnostics.
+Construction and resolution were corrected without loosening tolerances.
+Quadrature-node PASS counts are not scientific evidence beyond these checks.
+
+## N6 — Partial closure and escapes
+
+The permitted widths become small relative to energy in the formal running
+approximation. This leaves soft-photon dressing, a possible infraparticle,
+higher-order resummation and a microscopic phase open. Coincident cones,
+forbidden directions and zero coupling escape the displayed decay mechanism.
+
+## N7 — Steelman
+
+A criticism that a vanishing relative width proves no isolated pole is correct.
+Likewise a real velocity beta function alone is insufficient for stability.
+The note computes an additional necessary diagnostic and makes neither claim.
+No universal particle-instability conclusion survives these restrictions.
+
+## N8 — Prior comparison
+
+Vacuum Cherenkov emission and photon decay are established. The local delta
+is their explicit canonical anisotropic tensor/cap application to this quartet,
+including its Weyl count and the analytic shear-boundary coefficient. This
+is not a claim of first discovery of Lorentz-violating decay or a TOE prediction.
