+# Personal route review: visible threshold on real-overlap momenta
+
+2026-09-16 UTC. Author review only, not independent review or audit.
+
+The question was whether the source-dependent dark interval from Block10
+should be expected at all momenta. The answer proved here is positive source
+weight arbitrarily near the full threshold on a different stated slice.
+
+1. Alternative routes include exact diagonalization of a reducing sector,
+   resolvent continuation, source cyclicity and positivity. The last route
+   succeeds here; algebraic cyclicity is not assumed.
+2. The diagonal-line obstruction uses a conserved word-color count. It is
+   not a vacuum-independent or all-momentum obstruction. The present two-letter
+   space contains a positive slow texture, with no excursion to its orthogonal
+   third letter.
+3. The hidden phase condition is <u,v> real and nonnegative. The claim names
+   it explicitly. A generic complex overlap cannot be made simultaneously
+   positive at both endpoints by the same alphabet rotation.
+4. The original local source and the native signed translation frame are
+   retained. A momentum-dependent basis for proving positivity does not alter
+   the physical preparation. The boundary representation remains supplied.
+5. The result gives the infimum of source spectral support, not an isolated
+   band, threshold exponent or uniform lower amount of spectral weight.
+6. The constructive closure is the positive binary texture plus heat-semigroup
+   domination. Generic complex momenta, the periodic state and a physical
+   vacuum selector remain open.
+7. The strongest competing explanation is destructive endpoint interference
+   away from this slice. The proof does not exclude it or replace the earlier
+   near-diagonal upper leakage estimate by an unjustified lower bound.
+8. The J=0 two-half-line spectrum and the absence of any threshold eigenvector
+   were already established in Blocks9--10. They are dependencies/context,
+   not recounted as new discoveries. The new point is access by the SAME
+   local symmetric source at the positive-J real-overlap momenta.
+
+Proof review checked the binary reducing space, the c=0 connectivity endpoint,
+the tensor product overlap including both endpoint factors, and the positive
+Dyson expansion around the unbounded direct-sum swap Laplacian. Its endpoint
+perturbation is bounded. The domination constant is allowed to depend on the
