+# Frontier reassessment after the exclusion and cofactor mechanisms
+
+Personal working assessment, 2026-09-15. No axiom verdict or physical
+field-scaling conclusion follows from this checkpoint.
+
+The signed-loop route now accommodates the full same-species Gaussian,
+actual support exclusion, its softened forest version, and the complete
+local-resource sum for a prescribed exclusion derivative graph. The resource
+cost remains linear in component mass and derivative degrees contribute
+square roots of factorials. These solve specific implementation-independent
+proof obligations. They do not enumerate the full physical connected family.
+
+Two remaining problems are genuinely different: non-cycle mixed phase factors
+need a representation preserving signed spatial cancellation, and branching
+needs the physical graph multiplicities and source bounds at activity one.
+An arbitrary bounded residual is insufficient, as the retained Hadamard
+control showed. A second unrestricted forest on an already counted loop has
+more than exponentially many labelled choices; its factorial normalization
+cannot be spent twice.
+
+A useful uncompleted next calculation concerns same-species Gaussian
+DERIVATIVES. On the infinite four-dimensional cubic lattice, the scalar
+Laplacian symbol satisfies lambda(p)>=4|p|^2/pi^2 for p in [-pi,pi]^4.
+For a finite cochain j, put m=||j||_1 and r=||j||_2<=m. Split its Green
+energy at Fourier radius R with R^2=r/m<=1. On the low-frequency ball,
+|jhat|<=m and direct integration of |p|^-2 gives m^2 R^2/64. On its
+complement Parseval gives (pi^2/4)r^2/R^2. Consequently the proposed bound is
+
+    <j,G j> <= (pi^2/4+1/64) m r.
+
+The sum over finitely many cochain orientations obeys the same estimate
+when m includes every orientation. This direct Fourier argument should be
+checked against the exact cochain Laplacian conventions before use. The
+HLS literature search was only routing; no unread theorem is imported.
+
+If used for feature vectors sqrt(x)(G-I/32)^(1/2)j, their degree-d norm
+cost is at most C^d x^(d/2) m^(d/2) r^(d/2). Separate linear-mass and
+quadratic-current reserves would absorb this with roughly (d!)^(3/4),
+not the much worse crude filling-area moments. Such feature registers could
+extend the cofactor source lemma to prescribed Gaussian derivative graphs.
+The missing mixed residual and physical graph enumeration would still remain.
+This is a recorded attack direction, not a completed source theorem.
+
+The original portfolio also ranked native formation/probability selection.
+Current main's newly integrated formation-order classification is still an
+explicitly supplied binary sequential construction, not two full-axiom worlds.
+The existing priority-formation theorem provides an infinite bounded-degree
+construction but uses a finite prepared menu. A potentially higher-value next
+question is whether one can construct two complete covariant M2(C)-domain
+laws, with actual global permanent-record realizations and distinct readable
+conditional statistics, under the same current four axioms and primitives.
+That requires checking the full-domain meaning, possibility naturality,
+formation versus ongoing support, and state-versus-law distinction. It must
+not be replaced by another conditional menu or order comparison.
