+# Block5 scope and adversarial no-go review
+
+Personal N1-N8 review, 2026-09-15, under the previously pinned no-go skill
+SHA256 9020ba5c2797d8f026ddb72871b13f18a18cad4e0ec326c0f4653ceb438751bc,
+matching current main2ed54cb. No independent audit is claimed.
+
+Disposition: the conditional support theorems and positive kernels are
+preserved. A framework-wide claim that noncentral records are impossible,
+or that an axiom update is forced, FAILS: the internal naturality contract
+is not selected by the current axiom wording, a common-algebra/seed escape
+is explicitly constructed, and the physical kinetic realization is open.
+
+## N1 — actual mechanisms and outcomes
+
+| mechanism | object and intervention | outcome |
+|---|---|---|
+| invariant-probability support | explicit upper/lower unipotent conjugations on the full algebra; tightness without moment assumptions | every invariant probability is central; arbitrary supported scalar measures survive |
+| one-record stabilizer | distinct-eigenvalue scaling and Jordan unipotent cases | support is in C[A]; no unsupported generalization to two noncommuting records |
+| independent target relabeling | target automorphisms fix all input fibers | central output at every profile, conditional on this stronger action contract |
+| compact-subgroup comparison | circular entry Gaussian with supplied Hermitian norm | full support is possible under unitary conjugation; exact dilation variance ratio16 rejects full-inner invariance |
+| record-word construction | Gaussian coefficients on all input words through length3 | full-domain continuous equivariant kernel, support exactly the generated algebra, ongoing support and global formation |
+| compatible initial-state escape | four seeded matrices and a positive-probability two-step extension | a new record has full-algebra conditional support; empty-start centrality is not a statement about every initial condition |
+| algebraic inverse-corner construction | add intrinsically defined inverse maps between spectral idempotent ranges | Borel full-support output at every noncommuting profile, including triangular ones; exact Gaussian non-tightness proves the lost continuity |
+
+These are actual algebraic, measure and process mechanisms, not a count of
+independent physical walls. No finite route census is called exhaustive of
+all axiom-compatible physical constructions.
+
+## N2 — hypothesis relations
+
+Independent-fiber naturality is stronger than simultaneous naturality and
+cannot be treated as a second independent obstruction. The compact-group
