+# Author milestone review and next-obligation decision
+
+2026-09-16 UTC. This review is by the campaign's sole author. There was no
+subagent, independent reviewer, audit verdict, retained-grade promotion or
+main merge. The user extended the active work window to2026-09-16 13:45:03 UTC;
+packaging this milestone does not end that window.
+
+## What this package actually contributes
+
+README.md routes the packet into six scientific review units. The most useful
+completed bridges are the fixed-coupling cyclic equilibrium/rotor state
+construction, the explicit periodic holonomy analysis and fixed-box slow
+spectrum, the iterated local Maxwell/matter comparator, and the boundedness
+of the complete mixed native sixth-order kernel. Their mathematical premises
+and open review status remain explicit.
+
+The last review added an exact integer-cycle derivation of the periodic
+harmonic metric W_E/L. It also completed a positive-weight construction
+matching the free photon and Weyl cones, exact physical response identities
+which distinguish a photon witness from screened static twists, and a
+positive-J local-source access theorem on a second momentum slice.
+
+These are results in supplied models. They do not connect all sectors into
+one selected framework law. A common algebraic carrier, a positive history
+representation, a free cone match and a conditional continuum calculation
+are different claims and are not composed into a TOE by proximity in this
+packet.
+
+## Review coverage and limits
+
+During discovery the author read and reviewed each block's written derivation,
+its declared finite challenges and its failure records. The end-stage pass
+reread the load-bearing native sixth-order argument and Blocks15--22, then
+reviewed the new Blocks23--25. It also revisited the signed cut completion,
+contact-resource sum, positive auxiliary representation, formation naturality
+and support constraints, the polarized word/source proofs, and the conditional
+quadratic metric calculation. This is not a new independent audit of every
+historical supporting file or every imported source theorem.
+
+The current science workflow was reread. The base main revision is
+6ad6a2184b7c2067e597528e0964753874493b4a; later mathematical inputs were read
+at pinned revisions. A fresh fetch during this pass still gives
+e0ef7cf4633034a8c1e6d57f5812cc4275bf1349 as origin/main. The nine newly
+integrated September9 canonical native notes were read in full; their older
+supporting archives were not fully re-audited. END_STAGE_NEW_MAIN_READING.json
+binds those canonical bytes. Their arithmetic/propagation tasks do not reopen
+the later September13 positive Ward scalar result.
+
+Each block's PERSONAL_REVIEW receipt binds its actual note, runner and output
+bytes. A separate milestone manifest checks those bindings and the review map's
+local links. Hash agreement authenticates bytes, not mathematics. Finite
+checks were selected to challenge signs, domains, multiplicities, source
+normalization or a load-bearing calculation. Shared fixtures are declared;
+multiple outputs by one author do not establish independence.
+
+## Consequential corrections and retained failures
+
+- Fixed-order diagram work retains its failed cancellation/majorant routes.
+  A divergent bound is not asserted to be a divergent physical observable.
+- Formation constructions do not satisfy every approved kinetic-primitive
+  matching obligation. A framework-wide nonselection/no-go claim was rejected.
+- The word-spectrum runner's original precision loss and compensated-sum
+  repair retain the original tolerance and failure output.
+- Cyclic spectral checks retain both an iterative-solver stall and a sparse
+  solver's missed degenerate level. Complete number-sector diagonalization
+  repaired the latter; a small residual alone was insufficient.
+- Block20 retains its initial derivative-array shape exception. Block21
+  retains its initial Fourier-convention record and its literal-integration
+  dtype exception. The convention was aligned with the declared derivative,
+  and a separate Fourier integral was added.
+- Block22 explicitly supplies the additional energy-form argument needed
+  for single-field vector convergence; bounded characteristic convergence
+  alone was not promoted to arbitrary unbounded moment convergence.
+- Block24's author review replaced ordinary connected variance by inelastic
+  variance with the FULL ground-space projection removed. Its initial prose
+  is preserved. Hard-cutoff magnetic commutator boundary discrepancies are
+  reported, while the smooth rotor identity is tested on an interior core.
+
+No tolerance or scientific target was quietly relaxed to obtain a passing
+result. The individual notes delimit what each repair and check establishes.
+
+## Claims which must not appear in the milestone PR
+
+No full fixed-clock characteristic-functional limit at fixed finite N has
+been proved. Physical branching/residual-phase summation and state matching
+remain open. The positive auxiliary representation returns to a smoothed
+dual clock field, rather than solving that problem.
+
+No native sixth-order coefficient singularity is declared an exact physical
+singularity or a failure of the framework. A joint active/spectator treatment,
+energy dependence and resummation remain available. The current native star
+operator parent already supplies a double-compressed low-energy theorem;
+high-energy leakage, the extensive sum and a reorganized interacting state
+are still substantive obligations.
+
+No thermodynamic charged Coulomb/Weyl phase at fixed positive g follows from
+the fixed-box spectral theorem or its iterated g->0 then L->infinity state.
+The chosen positive weight match is not a selection mechanism. Exact Ward
+identities and flat external-twist screening do not by themselves prove a
+massless photon. A continuum spacing limit and a finite-payload rate remain
+separate from those statements.
+
